$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Stationary unstructured Voordelta demonstration
$ Coordinates: Amersfoort / RD New (EPSG:28992), vertical datum: NAP
$ Domain: x=20-85 km, y=380-450 km; water level fixed at NAP
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------

PROJECT 'VORDUNST' '001'
SET LEVEL 0.0 NAUTICAL
MODE STATIONARY TWODIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

$ The Triangle files are generated by generate_mesh.py. The default 200 m
$ mesh contains 114,426 vertices and 227,500 counterclockwise triangles.
CGRID UNSTRUCTURED CIRCLE 36 0.04 1.0 24
READGRID UNSTRUCTURED TRIANGLE 'voordelta_unstructured'

$ Bathymetry grid: 250 m, positive water depth relative to NAP.
$ Reuse the public-data-derived input from the regular Voordelta example.
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 20000.0 380000.0 0.0 260 280 250.0 250.0 &
        EXCEPTION -999.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 '../voordelta/voordelta.dep' 3 0 FREE

$ Synthetic stationary westerly storm, identical to the regular example.
$ Boundary marker 1 is the complete western side in the Triangle .node file.
WIND 15.0 270.0
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE 1 CONSTANT PAR 2.0 7.5 270.0 25.0

GEN3 KOMEN
BREAKING CONSTANT 1.0 0.73
FRICTION JONSWAP CONSTANT 0.038

$ Interpolate unstructured results to the same 500 m map as the regular case.
FRAME 'MAP' 20000.0 380000.0 0.0 65000.0 70000.0 130 140
BLOCK 'MAP' NOHEADER 'voordelta_depth.blk' LAYOUT 3 DEPTH
BLOCK 'MAP' NOHEADER 'voordelta_hs.blk' LAYOUT 3 HSIGN
POINTS 'SITES' 30000.0 430000.0 45000.0 420000.0 55000.0 440000.0
TABLE 'SITES' HEADER 'voordelta_sites.tbl' XP YP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 DIR

COMPUTE
STOP

